{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/653248-overly-generous-pacts","id":653248,"title":"overly generous pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-05T17:58:42-07:00","id":653248,"title":"overly generous pacts","content":"I just got Descent and I'm left wondering ... what keeps demons from just being overly generous* with the mortal side of the pact? It's not like it costs them anything, other than maybe further wiggle room for latter bargains. On the other hand it lowers the cost and makes it easier to convince a mortal to agree. Plus it makes a cultist more powerful and useful.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm missing something, but this just doesn't seem to mesh with the fluff of demons trying to be miserly with pacts and &quot;few demons give more than they take&quot;. It just feels like there should be some additional cost ... like maybe the larger the mortal benefit, the more likely the God Machine is to notice the mortal. <br /> <br /> *&quot;sure, 3 dots in every skill. Why not. Oh, and money, fame, beauty, and ... would you like to know kung fu?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T19:48:55-07:00","id":653410,"title":"","content":"I noticed that too, and house-ruled it. My rule: For pacts unbalanced in the favor of humans you have to make a Compromise roll, with a negative penalty equal to the amount of points the human side exceeds the demon's by. IE, if your pact with John Smith has him getting 9 points of benefits, and you're only taking 5 from him, you make a Compromise at a -4 penalty. The lore logic of this is that your Primum is being forced to do more with less, causing it to work harder, which is more noticeable.<br /> <br /> Then again, I view Descent Pacts as operating on similar fundamental rules to infernal pacts - you take something of metaphysical value, your Primum processes it and spits a benefit out, back to the original owner. You get to keep the shell that's left over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:37:23-07:00","id":653484,"title":"","content":"This topic will crop up from time to time.<br /> Here's the last one I recall, though there is a link on the first page to an earlier thread on the same subject.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/432735-pacts-weighted-towards-the-mortal\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/432735-pacts-weighted-towards-the-mortal\"> Pacts Weighted Towards the Mortal - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/432735-pacts-weighted-towards-the-mortal\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/432735-pacts-weighted-towards-the-mortal </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> There doesn't seem to be a drawback for just heaping your mortal with more and more stuff. Doesn't cost extra willpower. What's to stop a Demon from giving say his head cultist Resources 5 every time they renew their Pact for another year of dedicated service? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The simplest reason would of course be that the universe is not necessarily going to be as merciful to let you try and power level an athlete who might never walk away into an unmatched Olympian billionaire with six doctorates that they earned in between their modelling career without throwing a rather massive curveball at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:19:15-07:00","id":654585,"title":"","content":"In the end, it comes down to <i>trust</i>.<br /> <br /> The very act of making a pact can quite easily reveal that you're a &quot;Demon&quot;, which can potentially be perilous to your Cover if your charge starts blabbing. Making pacts also gives the GM's agents a trail to follow back to the Demon, people who have come into something that they don't &quot;deserve&quot; is a giant red flag for a spy/agent. Finally, there's no guarantee that anyone who you give a weighted pact to will necessarily be loyal to your Demon or their mission. And any control any individual Demon has over an individual, the GM can do better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:27:40-07:00","id":654590,"title":"","content":"Some Demons play the long game. They give great pacts at first (like drug dealers) to set up the mark for a soul pact. For those not interested in soul pacts, there is a point where it is no longer advantageous mechanically for a pact to be weighted in favor of the other party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T23:05:45-07:00","id":654778,"title":"","content":"But it is always mechanically advantageous to favor the mortal, since you pay nothing, but you should be getting social modifiars to convince the mortal to sign the pact. Anyways, I follow the same houserule suggested by Inodiv","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T17:57:16-07:00","id":655745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/653248-overly-generous-pacts?p=654590#post654590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Demons play the long game. They give great pacts at first (like drug dealers) to set up the mark for a soul pact. For those not interested in soul pacts, there is a point where it is no longer advantageous mechanically for a pact to be weighted in favor of the other party.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. And demons aren't concerned with the mechanics of it. They don't want a mortal's life to be better just so they can weave a tattered memory or an eye color into their cover. if a demon starts acting like the universe is his personal charity it won't be long before the other demons hear about deals with the devil where the mortal is getting one up on him. Word spreads, the other demons have a harder time making deals since one line demon out there is having pacts fall into his lap. His cover gets compromised since every Tom, dick, and Harry is trying to find the guy that can make anything possible. The other demon think at best it's a power play, at worst its the god machine screwing with them. Better safe than sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:08:08-07:00","id":655807,"title":"","content":"Few people in the World of Darkness are in the habit of giving something away for nothing. Demons are no different\u2014they're <i>demons</i>. They're liars, manipulators, seducers extraordinaire. They gained their individuality in a moment of selfishness, which set them apart from their angelic brethren. Not all demons are soul-eating monstrosities, but by their very nature they exist in defiance of another's will. A demon who gives away lots of gifts with nothing to show for it might be a relatively benign demon, but severely lags behind the demons who make deals that greatly benefit them. That demon has less leverage to call upon, is almost certainly seen as naive or weak in demon society, and is probably a prime target for other demons.<br /> <br /> A few demons might want to enrich the lives of the people they truly care about. Fewer still are the demons who want to just make the World of Darkness a better place by sticking their necks out and working metaphysical favors with no thought of reciprocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:46:26-07:00","id":655869,"title":"","content":"I don't know about civies, but the GM is definitely going to notice when a person from the same city wins the lottery every week, etc. It isn't strictly necessary to compromise Cover. Packs of Angels investigating the city works to the same effect. Pacts cost willpower and are a vulnerability for Demons. Demons always lose when a pact is destroyed. A Demon isn't going to want a bunch of pacts that they have to safeguard that offer almost nothing. Technically, the points about why a Demon would offer such great deals answers the problem itself. The Demon is getting advantages. No matter how a pact is weighed a Demon always wins, so when a Demon keeps offering bargain pacts it is because a Demon wants to do it. You can bet the Demon always sees the deal even or advantaged towards the Demon. A &quot;benevolent&quot; Demon gets to feel warm and fuzzy inside. The most successful Demons will prefer to burn more Willpower to get everything they can out of a mark as mentioned by others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}